.TH "NOIRPASS" "1" "2026-11-25" "noirpass 1.0.2" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
noirpass \- Minimal on\-demand GPG\-backed freedesktop Secret Service
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBnoirpass\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fICOMMAND\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Minimal on\-demand GPG\-backed freedesktop Secret Service
.PP
When invoked without a subcommand, \fBnoirpass\fR starts the D\-Bus daemon and
claims \fBorg.freedesktop.secrets\fR on the session bus once the object tree
is ready. Persistent values are encrypted at rest with OpenPGP and decrypted
via \fBgpg\-agent\fR(1); temporary secrets in the \fBsession\fR collection
stay in zeroizing memory until deleted or daemon exit.
.PP
Configuration defaults come from \fBconfig.toml\fR (see
\fBnoirpass.toml\fR(5)).
.SH OPTIONS
\fB\-\-store\-dir\fR \fI<STORE_DIR>\fR
.RS
Directory for the metadata index and encrypted secret files.
.PP
Defaults to `$XDG_DATA_HOME/noirpass` (or `~/.local/share/noirpass`).
.PP
[env: \fBNOIRPASS_STORE\fR]
.RE
.PP
\fB\-\-idle\-exit\fR \fI<IDLE_EXIT>\fR
.RS
Exit after this many seconds without Noirpass application activity (0 = after
activity, \-1 = never).
.PP
The daemon only exits when there are also no open transport sessions and no
temporary secrets in the standard session collection. Defaults to
`config.toml` `idle_exit`, or 300 when omitted.
.RE
.PP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
.RS
Print help (see a summary with '\-h')
.RE
.PP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
.RS
Print version
.RE
.SH COMMANDS
.SS init
\fBnoirpass init\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.PP
Initialize noirpass with an exported public `OpenPGP` recipient cert
.PP
\fB\-\-recipient\fR \fI<RECIPIENT>\fR
.RS
Recipient cert path, or '\-' to read from stdin
.RE
.SS deinit
\fBnoirpass deinit\fR
.PP
Permanently delete all Noirpass\-owned state after two confirmations
.SS status
\fBnoirpass status\fR
.PP
Report whether the noirpass store is initialized and usable
.SS list
\fBnoirpass list\fR
.PP
List indexed secrets without decrypting them
.SS delete
\fBnoirpass delete\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fI<ID>\fR
.PP
Delete one indexed secret and its ciphertext file
.PP
\fIID\fR
.RS
Secret id shown by `noirpass list`
.RE
.PP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
.RS
Skip the interactive confirmation
.RE
.SS check
\fBnoirpass check\fR [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.PP
Check redb metadata against `.gpg` files and offer safe repair
.PP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
.RS
Delete stale/corrupt entries (including canonical ciphertext) and corrupt
aliases without prompting
.RE
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBNOIRPASS_STORE\fR
Overrides the store directory when \fB\-\-store\-dir\fR is not passed.
.TP
\fBXDG_DATA_HOME\fR
Base directory for the default store \fI$XDG_DATA_HOME/noirpass\fR when set to
an absolute path.
.TP
\fBHOME\fR
Fallback base directory for \fI~/.local/share/noirpass\fR when
\fBXDG_DATA_HOME\fR is unset.
.TP
\fBRUST_LOG\fR
Controls diagnostic log filtering via \fBtracing_subscriber\fR.
.TP
\fBDBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS\fR
Session bus socket used by the daemon.
.TP
\fBGNUPGHOME\fR
GnuPG home directory used when locating \fBgpg\-agent\fR(1).
.SH FILES
.TP
\fI$XDG_DATA_HOME/noirpass\fR
Default store directory (or \fI~/.local/share/noirpass\fR when
\fBXDG_DATA_HOME\fR is unset).
.TP
\fI<STORE_DIR>/config.toml\fR
Persisted store configuration and runtime settings. See
\fBnoirpass.toml\fR(5).
.TP
\fI<STORE_DIR>/keys/recipient.pgp\fR
Stored binary OpenPGP public certificate for the configured recipient.
.TP
\fI<STORE_DIR>/index.redb\fR
Metadata database for collections, aliases, and item attributes.
.TP
\fI<STORE_DIR>/secrets/\fR
Directory holding per\-item OpenPGP ciphertext files.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Exits \fB0\fR on success and a non\-zero status on configuration, store,
agent, D\-Bus, or confirmation failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBnoirpass.toml\fR(5), \fBgpg\fR(1), \fBgpg\-agent\fR(1), \fBsystemctl\fR(1)
